{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When connecting AI tools to databases, my first concern was who could see what. Necessary order data should remain readable, while separately managed settlements should stay protected by existing privileges."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "QueryPie Community includes an MCP server. With MCP Inspector, an order query succeeded while the same account’s settlement query was denied. Both appeared in QueryPie audits."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Starting with the Existing Developer Account"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I reused Demo Developer’s Read-Only/Select on Orders Control Lab, adding no privileges for MCP."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/community-mcp/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Reviewing Demo Developer’s read privileges.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Reviewing Demo Developer’s read privileges."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Orders were allowed and settlements restricted. I especially wanted to see that distinction survive the change to MCP."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Connecting MCP to the QueryPie Address"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "MCP connects tools such as AI clients to external service functions. I used MCP Inspector to inspect requests and responses directly."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I used Streamable HTTP at http://localhost:8000/api/mcp, the QueryPie lab on my Mac. No database password was required in the client."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/community-mcp/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Registering the QueryPie Community endpoint in the MCP client.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Registering the QueryPie Community endpoint in the MCP client."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The browser signed in as Demo Developer completed authentication and showed Connected. iam_user_me returned Demo Developer and demo-dev, confirming whose privileges applied."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/community-mcp/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Verifying the authenticated MCP user is Demo Developer.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Verifying the authenticated MCP user is Demo Developer."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Selecting the Orders Database from Permitted Connections"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "dac_list_accessible_connections returned Orders Control Lab and Orders Demo MySQL, the same two shown in the user interface."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/community-mcp/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Two database connections accessible to the current user.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Two database connections accessible to the current user."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The list included cluster_uuid for the next query. I passed Orders Control Lab’s value to the query tool, reusing registered connections and privileges."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Querying One Order"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In this version the tool was dac_query. I submitted SELECT for order 4003’s ID, status, and amount."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "attrs": {
        "language": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SELECT order_id, status, total_amount\nFROM orders_control.orders\nWHERE order_id = 4003;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "It returned one row: 4003, DELIVERED, 18500.00, confirming the earlier change through MCP too."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/community-mcp/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. One order returned through MCP.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. One order returned through MCP."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Same Connection Still Denies Settlements"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Using the same tool and connection, I selected settlement ID and amount for order 4002 from settlement_details."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "attrs": {
        "language": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SELECT settlement_id, order_id, settlement_amount\nFROM orders_control.settlement_details\nWHERE order_id = 4002;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Instead of data, the response reported missing table privileges. Access to orders did not open separately protected settlements."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/community-mcp/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. Existing access restrictions block the settlement query.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. Existing access restrictions block the settlement query."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "No MCP-specific settlement rule was needed. The same boundaries allowed useful reads and protected sensitive tables, avoiding a separate privilege model for each new tool."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Audit Records Identify MCP as the Source"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Audit → Databases → Query Audit contained both queries, each attributed to Demo Developer on Orders Control Lab."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The order read was Success, with Executed From MCP. Existing audits showed both person and access route."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/community-mcp/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. Order audit retains user, connection, and MCP source.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. Order audit retains user, connection, and MCP source."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The settlement request was Failure and Prevented, with SQL and the table-permission error in details. Administrators could verify the client’s denial result independently."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/community-mcp/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. Blocked settlement SQL and error retained in audit details.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. Blocked settlement SQL and error retained in audit details."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The familiar management after connection was the highlight. MCP used the same users and database privileges, and SQL stayed in the same audit view. Existing access controls and audits can carry over to AI-tool integration."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7 and MCP Inspector 2.14.0. Direct tool calls verified authentication, orders, settlement blocking, and audits."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
